    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the title iv or unemployment work registration compliance exemption of the person applies.

rule paragraph_1_work_requirements_exemption_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)":
the paragraph 1 work requirements exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the care responsibility exemption of the person applies.

rule paragraph_1_work_requirements_exemption_applies_3 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)":
the paragraph 1 work requirements exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the bona fide student half time enrollment exemption of the person applies.

rule paragraph_1_work_requirements_exemption_applies_4 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)":
the paragraph 1 work requirements exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the treatment and rehabilitation program participation exemption of the person applies.

rule paragraph_1_work_requirements_exemption_applies_5 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)":
the paragraph 1 work requirements exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the employment or earnings exemption of the person applies.

rule paragraph_1_work_requirements_exemption_applies_6 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)":
the paragraph 1 work requirements exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the youth work requirement exemption of the person applies.

rule subject_work_requirement_failure_counts_as_paragraph_1_failure with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(A)":
a person is subject work requirement failure counts as paragraph 1 failure if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is subject work requirement noncompliance treated as paragraph 1 failure.

rule state_may_lower_dependent_child_age_for_care_responsibility_exemption with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)":
the state of a person may lower dependent child age for care responsibility exemption if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is state requested waiver to lower subparagraph b age
        and the person is secretary denied waiver as of august 1 1996
        and the years since state lowered age of the person is a number N
        and the waiver lower age option max period years is a number M
        and N <= M
        and the lowered dependent child age years of the person is a number K
        and the waiver lower age option min child age years is a number P
        and K >= P
        and the lowered dependent child age years of the person is a number Q
        and the waiver lower age option max child age years is a number R
        and Q <= R.

